(7564619, 1213096, 96751, '<td valign="top">Love that the lens warp makes it look like it''s leaning into the storm.</td>', 'Love that the lens warp makes it look like it''s leaning into the storm.', '2018-04-02 11:28:10.000000', NULL, 0),
(7564620, 1213195, 128323, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by tanguera:</b></div><hr/><i> Amazing. Is it always this empty? Or were you just exceedingly lucky? </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>The center square area is always empty when visitors are allowed.  People do tend to walk a few feet into the square (barefoot) to take pictures, then the security guards eventually shoo them back off of the tile.  The visitors are confined to walking around the edges, and into some of the larger prayer rooms within the area under the big domes.<br/> <br/>If anyone ever visits Abu Dhabi, this should be a high priority to go see.  Security is tight, but it''s quick to get in, and best of all it''s free!</td>', 'Originally posted by tanguera: Amazing. Is it always this empty? Or were you just exceedingly lucky?   The center square area is always empty when visitors are allowed.  People do tend to walk a few feet into the square (barefoot) to take pictures, then the security guards eventually shoo them back off of the tile.  The visitors are confined to walking around the edges, and into some of the larger prayer rooms within the area under the big domes. If anyone ever visits Abu Dhabi, this should be a high priority to go see.  Security is tight, but it''s quick to get in, and best of all it''s free!', '2018-04-02 11:30:22.000000', NULL, 0),
(7564621, 1213090, 109387, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by tanguera:</b></div><hr/><i> I think you''re addicted to this place.<br/> <br/>Or maybe live here :) </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>There are several of them Johanna. I couldn''t have taken too many shots there, I want to this one only twice. They are called Trabocco and some of them are still used to fish.</td>', 'Originally posted by tanguera: I think you''re addicted to this place. Or maybe live here :)   There are several of them Johanna. I couldn''t have taken too many shots there, I want to this one only twice. They are called Trabocco and some of them are still used to fish.', '2018-04-02 11:34:20.000000', NULL, 0),
