(7564635, 1212882, 25024, '<td valign="top">Hello from the critique club<br/> <br/>An appealing image that fulfils the challenge brief well<br/> <br/>I''m always gonna favour a nicely done reflection and this is done nicely, well done Harrison. Your composition is good with the well lit Chrysler building centre stage, this together with your patience to wait for a well timed action to complement the image has completed the overall effect very well.</td>', 'Hello from the critique club An appealing image that fulfils the challenge brief well I''m always gonna favour a nicely done reflection and this is done nicely, well done Harrison. Your composition is good with the well lit Chrysler building centre stage, this together with your patience to wait for a well timed action to complement the image has completed the overall effect very well.', '2018-04-02 13:35:36.000000', NULL, 0),
(7564636, 1213210, 25024, '<td valign="top">Hello from the critique club<br/> <br/>An appealing image that fulfils the challenge brief well<br/> <br/>You have chosen a famous landmark Janine well known to all your viewers. However, there is not really anything special about the image that makes it stand out from the crowd, probably quite difficult on the day but essential to really make it unique</td>', 'Hello from the critique club An appealing image that fulfils the challenge brief well You have chosen a famous landmark Janine well known to all your viewers. However, there is not really anything special about the image that makes it stand out from the crowd, probably quite difficult on the day but essential to really make it unique', '2018-04-02 13:38:39.000000', NULL, 0),
(7564646, 1212842, 60581, '<td valign="top">Sure, this location is other size of NYC. From this location there is another place called "Liberty State Park" we can go there and you can some nice city view, statue of liberty shots.<br/> <br/><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by tanguera:</b></div><hr/><i> I will have to visit this next time I''m in town. </i></td></tr></table> <br/></td>', 'Sure, this location is other size of NYC. From this location there is another place called "Liberty State Park" we can go there and you can some nice city view, statue of liberty shots. Originally posted by tanguera: I will have to visit this next time I''m in town.  ', '2018-04-02 17:05:40.000000', NULL, 0),
(7564648, 1212992, 19959, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by tanguera:</b></div><hr/><i> Very classical colors and sky.  Where did you take this from? I love that you included the other landmarks. </i></td></tr></table> - Thanks. This was taken from the ''typewriter'' building at the lower level (i.e. Not at the top of the glass elevator)<br/></td>', 'Originally posted by tanguera: Very classical colors and sky.  Where did you take this from? I love that you included the other landmarks.  - Thanks. This was taken from the ''typewriter'' building at the lower level (i.e. Not at the top of the glass elevator)', '2018-04-02 17:35:47.000000', NULL, 0),
(7564649, 1213220, 29269, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by tanguera:</b></div><hr/><i> Is the whole thing painted gold, or does it just look like that? </i></td></tr></table> <br/>Yes, it is gold indeed. Golden temple in Kyoto. The upper 2 stories are gold-plated, the bottom one is bamboo or some such thing. Something about Shoguns not liking the Emperor that lived on the 1st floor ;)<br/><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kinkaku-ji" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kinkaku-ji</a></td>', 'Originally posted by tanguera: Is the whole thing painted gold, or does it just look like that?  Yes, it is gold indeed. Golden temple in Kyoto. The upper 2 stories are gold-plated, the bottom one is bamboo or some such thing. Something about Shoguns not liking the Emperor that lived on the 1st floor ;)https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kinkaku-ji', '2018-04-02 17:36:34.000000', NULL, 0),
